{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l31fhrif","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline","year":2010,"examDate":2010,"subject":"physics","chapter":"simple-harmonic-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"simple-harmonic-motion","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pif-the-total-energy-of-the-particle-is-e-it-will-perform-jee-advanced-physics-magnetism-iniwkxabeukxbkwk","content":"<p>If the total energy of the particle is E, it will perform periodic motion only if</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"E < 0"},{"identifier":"B","content":"E > 0"},{"identifier":"C","content":"V<sub>0</sub> > E > 0"},{"identifier":"D","content":"E > V<sub>0</sub>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>The kinetic energy of the particle cannot be negative. The total energy E is the sum of the kinetic energy K(x) and potential energy V(x) i.e.,</p>\n<p>E = K(x) + V(x). ....... (1)</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31krb4q/31a8bfd6-9679-4f0e-9b5b-7af2521de1ad/3ac5eeb0-d128-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31krb4r.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l31krb4q/31a8bfd6-9679-4f0e-9b5b-7af2521de1ad/3ac5eeb0-d128-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31krb4r.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Simple Harmonic Motion Question 17 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l31krb4q/31a8bfd6-9679-4f0e-9b5b-7af2521de1ad/3ac5eeb0-d128-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31krb4r.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l31krb4q/31a8bfd6-9679-4f0e-9b5b-7af2521de1ad/3ac5eeb0-d128-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31krb4r.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31krb4q/31a8bfd6-9679-4f0e-9b5b-7af2521de1ad/3ac5eeb0-d128-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31krb4r.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l31krb4q/31a8bfd6-9679-4f0e-9b5b-7af2521de1ad/3ac5eeb0-d128-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31krb4r.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l31krb4q/31a8bfd6-9679-4f0e-9b5b-7af2521de1ad/3ac5eeb0-d128-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31krb4r.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l31krb4q/31a8bfd6-9679-4f0e-9b5b-7af2521de1ad/3ac5eeb0-d128-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31krb4r.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>From the given figure, V(x) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.312ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.751ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -636 778 774\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2265\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2265\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 0 for all x. If E <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.312ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.751ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -636 778 774\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2264\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2264\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 0 for some x then kinetic energy K(x) = E <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"current